<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eleanor of Arborea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1347–1404</span> · Also known as Eleonora d'Arborea, Eleonora of Arborea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eleanor of Arborea was a Sardinian ruler who governed the Judicate of Arborea for her young sons from 1383 until her death in 1404. Daughter of Mariano IV, she continued the war against the Crown of Aragon and in 1392 issued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carta-de-logu">Carta de Logu</a>, a law code in Sardinian that remained in force across the island until 1827. She is regarded as a Sardinian national heroine.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-arborea.jpg" alt="Eleanor of Arborea" width="320" height="504" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antonio Benini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elianora_de_Arbar%C3%A8e.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
